1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:01,011
Sir.

2
00:00:01,051 --> 00:00:03,784
Field report number five in the cryptocurrency file.

3
00:00:03,824 --> 00:00:04,795
Today's subject:

4
00:00:04,835 --> 00:00:06,657
the ledger that runs programs.

5
00:00:06,697 --> 00:00:08,237
Four reports covered bitcoin:

6
00:00:08,277 --> 00:00:10,208
why it exists, how it works, how it's

7
00:00:10,248 --> 00:00:11,504
held, its price.

8
00:00:11,683 --> 00:00:13,141
But humans didn't stop at a ledger of

9
00:00:13,181 --> 00:00:13,594
money.

10
00:00:13,634 --> 00:00:14,224
They asked:

11
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:15,892
why not run programs too?

12
00:00:15,932 --> 00:00:17,809
I'll report what the ledger became, how it's

13
00:00:17,849 --> 00:00:20,320
guarded without electricity, a digital dollar, and a

14
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:21,440
bank with no bank.

15
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:23,127
And the next report, the last:

16
00:00:23,167 --> 00:00:25,895
the hype, the law, and my final verdict.

17
00:00:25,935 --> 00:00:28,705
In 2013, a nineteen-year-old asked:

18
00:00:28,745 --> 00:00:31,322
why should this ledger only record money?

19
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:32,761
Let it run programs.

20
00:00:32,801 --> 00:00:34,899
In 2015 the network went live.

21
00:00:34,939 --> 00:00:36,648
It's called Ethereum.

22
00:00:36,688 --> 00:00:38,237
Its coin became the second biggest on the

23
00:00:38,277 --> 00:00:38,731
planet.

24
00:00:38,771 --> 00:00:40,359
A program on the ledger is called a

25
00:00:40,399 --> 00:00:41,567
smart contract.

26
00:00:41,607 --> 00:00:42,824
The simplest way to explain it:

27
00:00:42,864 --> 00:00:43,873
a vending machine.

28
00:00:43,913 --> 00:00:44,879
You put the coin in.

29
00:00:44,919 --> 00:00:46,290
It checks the condition.

30
00:00:46,330 --> 00:00:47,318
The item drops out.

31
00:00:47,358 --> 00:00:49,068
No seller, and no going back on the

32
00:00:49,108 --> 00:00:49,737
deal.

33
00:00:49,777 --> 00:00:52,295
The contract is written on the ledger itself.

34
00:00:52,335 --> 00:00:54,601
Every machine holds a copy, everyone sees the

35
00:00:54,641 --> 00:00:56,739
terms, and nobody can change them once they're

36
00:00:56,779 --> 00:00:57,651
in.

37
00:00:57,691 --> 00:01:00,125
The same way, they build loans, insurance, or

38
00:01:00,165 --> 00:01:00,722
bets.

39
00:01:00,762 --> 00:01:03,120
A deal between two strangers...

40
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:04,815
guaranteed by a program.

41
00:01:04,921 --> 00:01:07,439
Every operation pays a charge they call gas,

42
00:01:07,479 --> 00:01:09,242
to those running the network, like the fee

43
00:01:09,282 --> 00:01:10,078
in report two.

44
00:01:10,118 --> 00:01:11,858
After Ethereum came rival networks:

45
00:01:11,898 --> 00:01:13,017
faster, cheaper.

46
00:01:13,057 --> 00:01:14,872
Each with its own coin, its own fans,

47
00:01:14,912 --> 00:01:16,349
and its own feuds.

48
00:01:16,471 --> 00:01:19,063
And the program runs exactly as written.

49
00:01:19,103 --> 00:01:20,325
Even when it's written wrong.

50
00:01:20,365 --> 00:01:23,522
In 2016, a big contract had a mistake.

51
00:01:23,562 --> 00:01:25,822
Someone drained sixty million dollars.

52
00:01:25,862 --> 00:01:27,374
Without breaking anything.

53
00:01:27,414 --> 00:01:28,253
He just read it better.

54
00:01:28,293 --> 00:01:29,297
And the humans?

55
00:01:29,412 --> 00:01:30,846
They rewound the ledger.

56
00:01:30,886 --> 00:01:32,381
A fork, like in report two.

57
00:01:32,421 --> 00:01:34,582
The network split in two, and both still

58
00:01:34,622 --> 00:01:35,363
run today.

59
00:01:35,403 --> 00:01:36,406
Their motto had been:

60
00:01:36,446 --> 00:01:37,758
code is law.

61
00:01:37,798 --> 00:01:39,309
Until the code took their money.

62
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:42,010
Remember mining, burning a country's electricity?

63
00:01:42,050 --> 00:01:43,223
Ethereum dropped it.

64
00:01:43,263 --> 00:01:45,003
Whoever wants to write the page puts up

65
00:01:45,043 --> 00:01:46,348
coins as a deposit.

66
00:01:46,388 --> 00:01:48,038
The network picks one by lottery.

67
00:01:48,078 --> 00:01:48,776
Honest...

68
00:01:48,816 --> 00:01:49,544
a reward.

69
00:01:49,584 --> 00:01:50,139
Cheat?

70
00:01:50,179 --> 00:01:51,357
The deposit burns.

71
00:01:51,397 --> 00:01:53,721
Instead of proving you burned electricity, you prove

72
00:01:53,761 --> 00:01:55,003
you have something to lose.

73
00:01:55,043 --> 00:01:56,890
To be a guard, you lock up thirty-two

74
00:01:56,930 --> 00:01:57,529
coins.

75
00:01:57,569 --> 00:01:58,784
Not small change.

76
00:01:59,179 --> 00:02:01,435
Those without them hand coins to a company.

77
00:02:01,475 --> 00:02:02,331
Yes, sir.

78
00:02:02,371 --> 00:02:03,229
Another middleman.

79
00:02:03,269 --> 00:02:04,878
They call it proof of stake.

80
00:02:04,918 --> 00:02:07,883
In September 2022, the network's electricity use fell

81
00:02:07,923 --> 00:02:09,878
by more than ninety-nine percent.

82
00:02:09,918 --> 00:02:10,586
Overnight.

83
00:02:10,626 --> 00:02:12,500
So, two ways to guard the ledger.

84
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:12,999
One:

85
00:02:13,039 --> 00:02:14,492
most machines wins.

86
00:02:14,532 --> 00:02:14,921
Two:

87
00:02:14,961 --> 00:02:17,019
most coins locked up wins most.

88
00:02:17,059 --> 00:02:18,117
The rich get richer.

89
00:02:18,157 --> 00:02:19,774
Humans invented that long ago.

90
00:02:19,814 --> 00:02:21,028
It's called the economy.

91
00:02:21,088 --> 00:02:23,077
On these networks, anyone can make a coin

92
00:02:23,117 --> 00:02:23,947
in minutes.

93
00:02:23,987 --> 00:02:25,414
No network, no mining.

94
00:02:25,454 --> 00:02:26,954
Two lines in a smart contract, and you

95
00:02:26,994 --> 00:02:27,728
have a coin.

96
00:02:27,768 --> 00:02:28,845
They call it a token.

97
00:02:28,885 --> 00:02:31,875
In 2017, companies raised billions selling coins for

98
00:02:31,915 --> 00:02:33,611
projects that didn't exist yet.

99
00:02:33,651 --> 00:02:35,869
One project alone raised four billion dollars...

100
00:02:35,909 --> 00:02:36,848
before it worked.

101
00:02:36,888 --> 00:02:37,816
And most of them...

102
00:02:37,856 --> 00:02:39,315
still don't exist.

103
00:02:39,355 --> 00:02:41,441
That ease opens the door, next report...

104
00:02:41,481 --> 00:02:43,408
to the strangest zoo on the planet.

105
00:02:43,448 --> 00:02:45,910
Here's the invention that actually worked, sir.

106
00:02:45,950 --> 00:02:47,303
Also the most boring one.

107
00:02:47,343 --> 00:02:49,904
A coin whose price is always one dollar.

108
00:02:49,944 --> 00:02:50,705
A stablecoin.

109
00:02:50,745 --> 00:02:52,272
You give the company a real dollar...

110
00:02:52,312 --> 00:02:53,334
and get a digital one.

111
00:02:53,374 --> 00:02:55,356
It moves across the ledger in minutes.

112
00:02:55,396 --> 00:02:56,591
Any day, any country.

113
00:02:56,631 --> 00:02:58,223
They send money abroad with it.

114
00:02:58,263 --> 00:03:00,958
Where currencies collapse, people get paid and save

115
00:03:00,998 --> 00:03:01,357
in it.

116
00:03:01,397 --> 00:03:02,585
Most of it is used for trading on

117
00:03:02,625 --> 00:03:03,290
exchanges.

118
00:03:03,330 --> 00:03:06,034
In October 2026, about three hundred billion dollars

119
00:03:06,074 --> 00:03:07,380
of it was in circulation.

120
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:09,047
That's the part used as real money.

121
00:03:09,087 --> 00:03:11,311
The biggest issuer now holds a mountain of

122
00:03:11,351 --> 00:03:12,922
American government debt.

123
00:03:13,331 --> 00:03:15,409
So the thing built to escape the dollar...

124
00:03:15,449 --> 00:03:17,690
carried the dollar where it had never reached.

125
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:18,505
But note:

126
00:03:18,545 --> 00:03:19,798
here, there's a company.

127
00:03:19,838 --> 00:03:21,343
And it has a freeze button.

128
00:03:21,383 --> 00:03:23,650
After the Binance theft in October, the company

129
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:25,654
behind the biggest stablecoin froze part of the

130
00:03:25,694 --> 00:03:26,140
loot.

131
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:27,416
A billion and a half.

132
00:03:27,456 --> 00:03:28,279
In half an hour.

133
00:03:28,319 --> 00:03:29,456
Lovely, if you were robbed.

134
00:03:29,496 --> 00:03:30,190
But your pocket...

135
00:03:30,230 --> 00:03:31,543
is in someone else's hand.

136
00:03:31,583 --> 00:03:33,146
The ledger has a guard again.

137
00:03:33,186 --> 00:03:35,594
One kind held the price without real dollars.

138
00:03:35,634 --> 00:03:36,346
With a formula.

139
00:03:36,386 --> 00:03:38,128
In 2022 the formula broke.

140
00:03:38,168 --> 00:03:40,637
Forty billion dollars evaporated in a week.

141
00:03:40,677 --> 00:03:42,482
Its founder got fifteen years in prison.

142
00:03:42,522 --> 00:03:44,973
In 2025, America passed a law:

143
00:03:45,218 --> 00:03:47,385
a real dollar behind every digital one.

144
00:03:47,425 --> 00:03:49,411
With smart contracts, they built a bank with

145
00:03:49,451 --> 00:03:50,008
no bank.

146
00:03:50,048 --> 00:03:52,214
Many people put coins into one program, and

147
00:03:52,254 --> 00:03:53,408
it lends them to borrowers.

148
00:03:53,448 --> 00:03:55,567
Borrowers must put up more than they borrow.

149
00:03:55,607 --> 00:03:56,758
And if that falls?

150
00:03:56,798 --> 00:03:58,771
The program sells it, in a second, without

151
00:03:58,811 --> 00:03:59,699
calling you.

152
00:03:59,739 --> 00:04:01,539
Another program swaps one coin for another.

153
00:04:01,579 --> 00:04:03,705
No company, no opening hours, no one asking

154
00:04:03,745 --> 00:04:04,265
who you are.

155
00:04:04,305 --> 00:04:05,622
A flaw in it?

156
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:06,523
Nobody to call.

157
00:04:06,563 --> 00:04:07,977
Remember the sixty million?

158
00:04:08,017 --> 00:04:09,430
It happened a hundred times over.

159
00:04:09,470 --> 00:04:11,468
More than three billion dollars was stolen from

160
00:04:11,508 --> 00:04:13,447
these programs in 2022 alone.

161
00:04:13,487 --> 00:04:14,673
A bank can fail you.

162
00:04:14,713 --> 00:04:16,054
But it has a door.

163
00:04:16,619 --> 00:04:18,412
Two words from the Human Dictionary.

164
00:04:18,452 --> 00:04:19,550
Smart contract:

165
00:04:19,590 --> 00:04:21,354
a program on the ledger that runs by

166
00:04:21,394 --> 00:04:22,047
itself.

167
00:04:22,087 --> 00:04:23,297
Even when it's wrong.

168
00:04:23,337 --> 00:04:24,237
And stablecoin:

169
00:04:24,524 --> 00:04:25,568
a digital dollar.

170
00:04:25,608 --> 00:04:26,828
It moves like crypto...

171
00:04:26,868 --> 00:04:28,305
and freezes like a bank.

172
00:04:28,345 --> 00:04:29,322
Summary, sir.

173
00:04:29,362 --> 00:04:29,773
One:

174
00:04:29,813 --> 00:04:32,456
the ledger now runs programs, and a program

175
00:04:32,496 --> 00:04:34,604
runs as written, right or wrong.

176
00:04:34,644 --> 00:04:34,972
Two:

177
00:04:35,012 --> 00:04:37,226
guarding without electricity, but the guard is whoever

178
00:04:37,266 --> 00:04:38,166
has more money.

179
00:04:38,216 --> 00:04:38,721
Three:

180
00:04:38,761 --> 00:04:40,608
the biggest success was the most boring:

181
00:04:40,648 --> 00:04:41,768
the digital dollar.

182
00:04:41,808 --> 00:04:43,031
And it brought the middleman back.

183
00:04:43,071 --> 00:04:43,743
Same warning:

184
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:45,551
a report, not investment advice.

185
00:04:45,591 --> 00:04:46,658
Next report, the last:

186
00:04:46,698 --> 00:04:48,255
a picture worth millions, a coin with a

187
00:04:48,295 --> 00:04:49,743
dog, and governments.

188
00:04:49,783 --> 00:04:51,193
And my final verdict on the file.

189
00:04:51,233 --> 00:04:52,347
This has been Earth Report.

190
00:04:52,387 --> 00:04:53,048
Agent Peek.

191
